WEBVTT

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:02.247
<i>Welcome to Supermax Prison.</i>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:07.710
<i>This is the only prison in the world
that can suppress any kind of superpower.</i>

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.256
<i>As you all know,</i>

00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:15.385
not everyone with superpowers
becomes a superhero.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.639
People who use their powers
for evil become supervillains.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.560
And this is where
those scumbag villains end up!

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.477
Look around!

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:30.900
Just because you've developed powers
doesn't mean you can do what you please.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:31.943
Understand?

00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:38.032
How about I shred him up
and make him chicken feed?

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:44.372
Don't get carried away.

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:49.919
See?

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:54.507
Inmate number 0053839.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.593
Johnny Bolt, exit your cell.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.094
Sure thing.

00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:09.522
Johnny Boy, you breaking out?

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:12.650
The big boss
is throwing a party today, you know?

00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:15.153
I'm getting released, not breaking out.

00:03:15.236 --> 00:03:18.865
I've got a party tonight too, dude.
With my honey.

00:03:18.948 --> 00:03:20.366
Glad to hear it.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.952
See you on the outside sometime.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:28.374
The fuck you goin', Bolt?
I was gonna have your ass next.

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:31.002
Come on. How about it?

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.296
Get that dirty asshole outta my face.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.756
Come on--

00:03:36.841 --> 00:03:39.218
Fuckin' scum, pissing himself like that.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.388
Come on, Johnny.
The outside's waiting for you.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:45.975
That's right, Eric. It's time to roll.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.238
Johnny! So today's the day.

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.955
I'm sure I'll be
seeing you again soon, partner.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.625
Hate to disappoint you,
but I won't be back.

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:12.585
<i>This is the changing room.</i>

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.893
Restraint vest… Cover him.

00:04:31.062 --> 00:04:31.896
<i>Release.</i>

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:39.529
Freedom!

00:04:40.196 --> 00:04:41.197
Here.

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:44.033
The moment I've been waiting for.

00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:49.372
That thing's falling apart.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.082
You should really get a new one.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:53.084
That reeks!

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:55.920
They're trying to cut costs, you know.

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:59.966
They're happy just as long as
it keeps you guys from using your powers.

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:01.968
But that's this place's selling point.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.137
Even if we got new ones,

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.931
we'd have to update
the whole damn control system.

00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:08.599
That would be the perfect time

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.643
to break out of this place.

00:05:11.227 --> 00:05:13.521
We've got a backup system,
so that won't happen.

00:05:14.731 --> 00:05:17.734
<i>Inmate number 0053839.</i>

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:20.862
Johnny Bolt. No address. No occupation.

00:05:21.446 --> 00:05:24.615
Sentenced to eight months for
the misdemeanors of property damage

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:27.285
caused by
a precision voltage control device

00:05:27.368 --> 00:05:31.456
and destruction of intangible data due to
widespread electromagnetic interference.

00:05:32.206 --> 00:05:34.334
Having served your time,
you're being released.

00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:38.338
What's his superpower?

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:39.255
Warden?

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.132
Let me see.

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:44.093
He can generate and release electricity.

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:47.013
Is he a member of the Network?

00:05:47.096 --> 00:05:49.515
No. He's got no connections.

00:05:50.558 --> 00:05:51.934
Just a punk villain?

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.352
Approved.

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:55.605
<i>Don't come back.</i>

00:05:56.105 --> 00:05:57.065
Sure thing!

00:05:57.148 --> 00:06:01.194
On the outside, I'll behave like
a proper citizen with superpowers.

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:02.111
Out.

00:06:10.119 --> 00:06:11.871
What's all this about?

00:06:11.954 --> 00:06:13.956
It's that charity group.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.708
Some kind of celebration?

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.543
It's a gift from Mr. Matts.

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:18.461
Matts?

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:22.590
I'm sure even a small-time villain
like you has heard of him.

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:28.054
He's the world's most renowned
supervillain, Mr. Christopher Matts.

00:06:29.764 --> 00:06:33.059
Living here, you don't get
much news of the outside.

00:06:33.142 --> 00:06:36.979
Matts is also known as The Bastard.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:39.899
Oh, is that right? The Bastard?

00:06:39.982 --> 00:06:41.526
Don't act dumb.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.569
You caught me.

00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:47.740
Anyway, that stuff is all part
of a world way out of my reach.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.534
You're right about that.

00:06:51.035 --> 00:06:55.957
Some villains on the outside doing
charity work for villains in prison is…

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:57.959
pretty damn fishy.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.711
What will you do when you get out?

00:07:00.795 --> 00:07:02.922
I'm not sure.

00:07:03.005 --> 00:07:05.341
I'll think about it
after having a nice fuck.

00:07:07.051 --> 00:07:09.428
You're a lucky man
to have someone waiting for you.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:14.517
Farewell, my friend.

00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:41.294
Johnny!

00:07:41.377 --> 00:07:43.629
What a sight for sore eyes, my sweetie.

00:07:52.513 --> 00:07:53.848
Shit. I've got a hard-on.

00:07:54.557 --> 00:07:55.600
<i>You naughty boy.</i>

00:08:05.526 --> 00:08:06.360
See?

00:08:12.116 --> 00:08:14.285
Being on the outside is awesome!

00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:15.912
Don't you agree, Kasey?

00:08:16.537 --> 00:08:18.498
It's time to shift gears.

00:08:19.957 --> 00:08:20.791
Holy…

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.836
Damn, this is good.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.105
We're here!

00:09:16.597 --> 00:09:17.765
Johnny!

00:09:17.848 --> 00:09:18.849
Welcome back!

00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:19.767
Yeah!

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.352
You guys!

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:26.232
How the hell did you idiots get in here?

00:09:26.315 --> 00:09:29.318
Gimme a break!
We're supervillains, after all.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:30.278
Right?

00:09:30.861 --> 00:09:31.862
-Right!
-Right!

00:09:32.446 --> 00:09:33.322
Oh, really?

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.160
Here you go!

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.412
To celebrate your release.

00:09:39.495 --> 00:09:40.663
Right!

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.048
Here's to

00:09:51.132 --> 00:09:52.258
Mr. Matts!

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:58.014
Don't overdo it.

00:09:58.097 --> 00:10:00.308
Fuck off! Today, I will do as I please!

00:10:01.976 --> 00:10:04.562
Guess we owe this all
to the big boss, Matts.

00:10:04.645 --> 00:10:05.855
Say, who is that?

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:09.191
The Bastard. He's legendary.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:12.194
Legendary? That's going a little far.

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:16.198
He used to be a top villain,
but he's an old-timer now, right?

00:10:16.866 --> 00:10:17.700
Don't be stupid.

00:10:18.534 --> 00:10:20.620
The big boss is still plenty dangerous.

00:10:21.245 --> 00:10:23.414
Don't you know about Danny Dubrovny?

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:27.168
<i>From what I heard,</i>

00:10:27.251 --> 00:10:29.337
<i>Danny had gotten out
of the villain business</i>

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.881
<i>and into some dodgy real-estate scam.</i>

00:10:33.174 --> 00:10:36.719
<i>After getting an investment of
five million dollars out of the big boss,</i>

00:10:37.345 --> 00:10:39.221
<i>he suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:41.223
<i>A few years later,</i>

00:10:41.307 --> 00:10:42.850
<i>Danny had moved to Miami</i>

00:10:42.933 --> 00:10:45.645
<i>and was involved in some
Japanese business.</i>

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.814
<i>He had a woman
and was living the good life</i>

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:51.901
<i>all thanks to the money
he pinched from the big boss.</i>

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.153
<i>Then one day,</i>

00:10:55.071 --> 00:10:56.739
<i>something horrible
happened to his old pal.</i>

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:02.995
<i>It happened to his favorite hooker too.</i>

00:11:03.579 --> 00:11:05.623
<i>And to his dealer back in Baltimore.</i>

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.168
<i>His best friend.</i>

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:11.796
<i>His mother.</i>

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.299
<i>His half-brother who lived in California.</i>

00:11:16.884 --> 00:11:19.220
<i>Even everyone at his accounting firm.</i>

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.389
<i>Their heads exploded.</i>

00:11:21.472 --> 00:11:23.808
Hold on! It was all…

00:11:24.392 --> 00:11:27.103
You see, that's how The Bastard operates.

00:11:27.853 --> 00:11:28.771
Is this about Danny?

00:11:29.605 --> 00:11:32.650
Until he and his girlfriend escaped
to the boonies,

00:11:32.733 --> 00:11:34.819
241 people had been killed.

00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:37.405
But there's no evidence of who did it.

00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:39.490
241 people?

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:41.951
All of them were blown up remotely?

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.829
Is that his power?

00:11:45.663 --> 00:11:48.332
<i>After they'd been scared shitless,</i>

00:11:48.416 --> 00:11:50.334
<i>they knew how it would end for them.</i>

00:11:51.836 --> 00:11:53.587
Danny… It hurts!

00:11:54.088 --> 00:11:55.965
-It hurts!
-What's wrong?

00:11:56.048 --> 00:11:57.341
My head!

00:11:57.425 --> 00:12:00.177
It's like someone is pumping air into it!

00:12:00.261 --> 00:12:01.345
It hurts!

00:12:01.971 --> 00:12:04.557
No! Stop!

00:12:07.268 --> 00:12:08.561
God damn it!

00:12:08.644 --> 00:12:11.689
Matts! Kill me!

00:12:11.772 --> 00:12:13.023
I know you're after me!

00:12:13.107 --> 00:12:15.401
Kill me!

00:12:15.484 --> 00:12:16.861
Just kill me now!

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:30.249
Why the fuck would I grant you your wish?

00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:37.339
<i>That's The Bastard for you.</i>

00:12:42.052 --> 00:12:43.429
To Mr. Matts.

00:12:44.013 --> 00:12:46.557
Here's to the big boss's Network.

00:12:47.099 --> 00:12:51.729
I thought that
the villains Network was an urban legend.

00:12:52.521 --> 00:12:53.898
That's right.

00:12:53.981 --> 00:12:57.860
The legend is a secret system
that exists outside the real world.

00:12:58.527 --> 00:13:02.198
It's a shadow world that
second-rate lowlifes like you can't see.

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:05.284
Everyone that's a part of it
gets locked up here.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.453
He's the big boss of

00:13:07.536 --> 00:13:12.291
the supervillain Network that stretches
from the West Coast to the East Coast.

00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:15.669
Here's to Mr. Matts.

00:13:18.422 --> 00:13:20.883
You seem to be having fun, Warden.

00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:24.136
That's right. Thank you.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.305
Even the unruly scumbags

00:13:26.388 --> 00:13:28.891
are patiently waiting
until their sentences are over.

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:30.476
I'm glad to hear it.

00:13:30.559 --> 00:13:32.269
Most important for us is

00:13:32.353 --> 00:13:35.231
to value our connections
with our comrades.

00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:39.527
Well, well…

00:13:40.027 --> 00:13:42.196
Tell the big boss thanks from me.

00:13:42.279 --> 00:13:43.364
Certainly.

00:13:44.615 --> 00:13:45.491
By the way…

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:50.120
I heard a rumor that the big boss
was taking all the loot he's gained

00:13:50.204 --> 00:13:52.540
and going abroad with it.

00:13:54.708 --> 00:13:56.335
Nothing more than a rumor.

00:13:59.296 --> 00:14:00.673
<i>Bring some salsa!</i>

00:14:00.756 --> 00:14:02.299
You guys are drunk!

00:14:05.261 --> 00:14:07.304
What's that? I like your taste.

00:14:07.805 --> 00:14:09.640
I figured you would.

00:14:10.266 --> 00:14:12.518
I told you, Kismet.

00:14:12.601 --> 00:14:14.520
Johnny knows what good taste is.

00:14:14.603 --> 00:14:18.816
Whenever I wear gold and shit like that,

00:14:19.441 --> 00:14:22.361
I always think
it will get snatched off me.

00:14:23.237 --> 00:14:25.322
That's 'cause you spread bad luck, dude.

00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:28.409
I can't help it. That's my power.

00:14:28.492 --> 00:14:30.536
I don't spread bad luck 'cause I want to.

00:14:30.619 --> 00:14:32.204
Yeah, right.

00:14:32.288 --> 00:14:33.789
Shut up, bad luck.

00:14:34.415 --> 00:14:37.084
Lately, we've had good luck.

00:14:37.585 --> 00:14:39.253
Really? What's up?

00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:44.842
We learned what it takes
to survive in this tech-driven society.

00:14:45.467 --> 00:14:49.513
It's more like we're slaves to tech
than people who learned how to use it.

00:14:50.055 --> 00:14:54.476
What? With our string of successes,
we've been lucky boys lately!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.811
Yeah, maybe so, but…

00:14:56.478 --> 00:15:00.190
To celebrate your return, Johnny,

00:15:00.274 --> 00:15:03.986
we've come up with a plan for a huge job.

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:05.321
Right!

00:15:06.488 --> 00:15:07.489
What kind of job?

00:15:10.618 --> 00:15:11.577
Let me show you.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.579
Hold on.

00:15:14.121 --> 00:15:17.499
If you-know-who hears this,
it'll cause us trouble.

00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.251
It's okay. Tell me about it.

00:15:19.335 --> 00:15:21.962
This place could be bugged too.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.384
Okay. This will knock your socks off.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.554
<i>Are you planning a bank heist?</i>

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:34.016
Cash is nothing but numbers.

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:37.102
What's more, its value changes every day.

00:15:37.186 --> 00:15:40.272
This is something
that doesn't change. Gemstones.

00:15:41.357 --> 00:15:42.900
Which store are we going after?

00:15:42.983 --> 00:15:46.195
Which store? That's a joke!
We're going after ten places

00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:47.821
in under ten minutes.

00:15:47.905 --> 00:15:49.531
<i>Ten places in ten minutes?</i>

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:51.533
<i>They're all close to one another.</i>

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:54.036
<i>It's possible if we go by motorcycle.</i>

00:15:54.119 --> 00:15:55.287
<i>Right!</i>

00:15:55.371 --> 00:15:58.248
The key is the number
of places and the time.

00:15:58.332 --> 00:16:01.794
We don't care
if we don't get much from each place.

00:16:01.877 --> 00:16:03.128
If we want to be greedy,

00:16:03.212 --> 00:16:06.298
we just increase
the number of places we hit.

00:16:10.177 --> 00:16:11.595
<i>Now I get it.</i>

00:16:11.679 --> 00:16:13.430
<i>If we hit that many all at once…</i>

00:16:13.931 --> 00:16:16.976
<i>It'll throw cops
and security companies into a panic.</i>

00:16:49.008 --> 00:16:52.177
<i>What's more, I think you know
that downtown San Francisco</i>

00:16:52.261 --> 00:16:54.346
<i>is one of the places in the US</i>

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.558
<i>with the lowest frequency of events
caused by superpowers.</i>

00:16:57.641 --> 00:16:58.475
<i>Which means…</i>

00:16:59.351 --> 00:17:00.769
<i>No heroes will interfere.</i>

00:17:04.148 --> 00:17:05.858
Each place in under a minute.

00:17:10.237 --> 00:17:11.280
That's seriously awesome!

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:12.448
Told ya!

00:17:12.531 --> 00:17:13.866
Whose plan is this?

00:17:13.949 --> 00:17:15.034
It was the Net--

00:17:15.117 --> 00:17:17.536
It was ours, obviously! Right?

00:17:17.619 --> 00:17:18.495
Right!

00:17:18.579 --> 00:17:20.622
You guys are geniuses!

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:21.999
I've had it with this!

00:17:22.916 --> 00:17:24.209
Kasey…

00:17:25.002 --> 00:17:29.423
If you hold tight
for a while and get a normal job,

00:17:29.506 --> 00:17:31.050
then a good job will come along.

00:17:31.633 --> 00:17:32.926
What kind of job would that be?

00:17:33.677 --> 00:17:35.637
Helping those veggie freaks?

00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:37.806
They're the decadent 1%.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.100
That's the jealousy of the 99%.

00:17:41.435 --> 00:17:42.269
<i>Hello.</i>

00:17:43.562 --> 00:17:45.856
<i>Welcome to an organic café
where you can enjoy</i>

00:17:45.939 --> 00:17:47.649
<i>the true flavor of vegetables,</i>

00:17:48.317 --> 00:17:50.110
<i>Green Green.</i>

00:17:50.694 --> 00:17:52.821
<i>Nearly all the food we get from</i>

00:17:52.905 --> 00:17:55.115
<i>local small farms
and the farmer's market is</i>

00:17:55.699 --> 00:17:57.493
<i>100% organic.</i>

00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:02.456
<i>We make the most of the ingredients,</i>

00:18:02.539 --> 00:18:07.169
<i>so you won't believe that
you're actually only eating vegetables.</i>

00:18:11.507 --> 00:18:14.718
You wanna work with those dilettantes too?

00:18:14.802 --> 00:18:15.636
Nah.

00:18:15.719 --> 00:18:19.139
See? And with you around,
this'll be a breeze.

00:18:19.223 --> 00:18:21.600
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:18:21.683 --> 00:18:23.477
Here's to Johnny the Bolt!

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.978
It'll be a breeze!

00:18:25.062 --> 00:18:25.896
Johnny!

00:18:28.982 --> 00:18:32.152
Say, you guys shouldn't get so drunk.

00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:34.321
What? What are you talking about?

00:18:34.822 --> 00:18:37.199
We're not done drinking yet.

00:18:37.282 --> 00:18:38.158
Right!

00:18:38.742 --> 00:18:40.077
But you know…

00:18:41.036 --> 00:18:43.831
See how hammered you are?

00:18:45.207 --> 00:18:46.416
Right.

00:19:01.348 --> 00:19:02.850
Now, come on, Johnny.

00:19:03.433 --> 00:19:05.269
Did you use your power?

00:19:07.479 --> 00:19:09.523
At last, we're alone.

00:19:11.108 --> 00:19:12.776
Such a naughty girl.

00:19:20.742 --> 00:19:21.660
I'm back.

00:19:22.744 --> 00:19:26.999
Everyone at Supermax Prison,
including the warden, Frank,

00:19:27.082 --> 00:19:28.876
sends their thanks.

00:19:30.085 --> 00:19:34.464
They say their ties with our Network
are heartfelt and sturdy.

00:19:36.258 --> 00:19:37.551
Mr. Matts?

00:19:39.178 --> 00:19:40.554
Can you understand it?

00:19:42.389 --> 00:19:44.057
Piet Mondrian, you mean?

00:19:44.975 --> 00:19:47.394
He says, "To live shrewdly in this world,

00:19:47.477 --> 00:19:51.690
one must always look
at the big picture and be objective."

00:19:52.482 --> 00:19:57.154
Mondrian's works
are known as abstract art.

00:19:57.738 --> 00:20:00.616
They're geometric, beautifully designed,

00:20:00.699 --> 00:20:05.245
and even now, 100 years later,
they're universally recognized.

00:20:06.038 --> 00:20:10.250
However, even with works
that look so abstract,

00:20:10.334 --> 00:20:15.172
some were influenced by
the objective real world.

00:20:15.881 --> 00:20:17.966
<i>Broadway Boogie Woogie</i>.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.427
It's a bird's-eye view of Manhattan,

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:23.680
a diagram of the gridwork
that divides up the city.

00:20:24.264 --> 00:20:25.307
In this diagram,

00:20:25.807 --> 00:20:29.937
you can feel the American music
the Dutch expatriate loved.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:34.691
Its beat and rhythm throb
through the city like nerve pulses.

00:20:34.775 --> 00:20:35.776
I see.

00:20:36.777 --> 00:20:41.031
In this world,
one needs a balanced rhythm.

00:20:41.114 --> 00:20:41.949
The Salamander.

00:20:42.616 --> 00:20:44.576
Yes, Mr. Matts?

00:20:45.535 --> 00:20:49.581
Everything is a matter
of cause and effect.

00:20:50.165 --> 00:20:52.793
<i>That's how the Network functions.</i>

00:21:06.723 --> 00:21:09.685
Well, I'll be pretty busy tomorrow.

00:21:09.768 --> 00:21:11.853
Hold on. You can't be serious.

00:21:11.937 --> 00:21:12.980
You bet I am.

00:21:13.063 --> 00:21:16.316
You'll join those idiots
in that plan they told you about?

00:21:16.984 --> 00:21:18.402
It's a good deal.

00:21:18.485 --> 00:21:22.030
I haven't worked in over six months,
so my wallet's pretty bare.

00:21:22.739 --> 00:21:25.158
So why don't you join us, Kasey?

00:21:25.242 --> 00:21:26.368
What?

00:21:26.451 --> 00:21:31.373
I mean, come on,
that power of yours is freaking awesome.

00:21:31.456 --> 00:21:32.666
No way.

00:21:32.749 --> 00:21:34.001
Aw, come on.

00:21:34.084 --> 00:21:36.128
I know full well you're a supervillain

00:21:36.211 --> 00:21:40.799
who's only interested in big games,
but do it to celebrate my release.

00:21:40.882 --> 00:21:41.800
Not a chance.

00:21:41.883 --> 00:21:45.512
Besides, do you know
who came up with that plan?

00:21:45.595 --> 00:21:46.596
Who?

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:48.307
The Network.

00:21:49.933 --> 00:21:53.061
It's a secret organization
of supervillains.

00:21:53.562 --> 00:21:54.688
Don't you know it?

00:21:54.771 --> 00:21:56.523
Oh… Well…

00:21:57.274 --> 00:21:58.900
Of course, I know it!

00:21:58.984 --> 00:22:03.280
For providing the plans,
they take a cut of the money.

00:22:03.864 --> 00:22:04.990
They always get their money.

00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.287
They're a criminal elite

00:22:10.370 --> 00:22:14.291
who make others do the dirty work
while building supervillain solidarity.

00:22:14.374 --> 00:22:16.001
This sounds fishy.

00:22:16.626 --> 00:22:19.796
Even if the jobs go perfectly,
they get a percentage of the take.

00:22:20.339 --> 00:22:21.423
Is that what you want?

00:22:22.132 --> 00:22:27.346
I'm not hiding by working with
those dilettantes because I want to.

00:22:27.429 --> 00:22:28.555
You know that.

00:22:28.638 --> 00:22:31.266
But we need excitement too, right?

00:22:31.349 --> 00:22:32.559
Yes, of course.

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:35.562
But idiotic excitement is costly.

00:22:36.063 --> 00:22:37.606
I want a life that's more stable.

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.067
Any work I do with supervillains

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:43.737
has to have a good balance
between the risks and the rewards.

00:22:45.238 --> 00:22:46.615
Balance?

00:22:46.698 --> 00:22:48.200
It's all about balance.

00:22:48.742 --> 00:22:52.621
To live smart, you've got to see
the whole picture and be more objective.

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:54.706
Live smart, huh?

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:59.711
Doing jewel heists with morons is not
what you do the day after your release.

00:23:00.879 --> 00:23:03.965
But we're supervillains, after all.

00:23:04.591 --> 00:23:07.761
If we had your power to deceive people,

00:23:08.345 --> 00:23:13.391
it would work better and be more reliable
than Kismet spreading bad luck.

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.312
Listen to me, Johnny.

00:23:18.855 --> 00:23:23.151
With your power,
you can do so many more wonderful things.

00:23:23.235 --> 00:23:24.361
Maybe so.

00:23:24.444 --> 00:23:25.737
I can tell.

00:23:27.155 --> 00:23:28.615
You and I should hide who we are

00:23:28.698 --> 00:23:31.910
until a far, far better chance
comes along.

00:23:32.494 --> 00:23:34.037
You see, you and I…

00:23:34.746 --> 00:23:35.580
Me and you…

00:23:36.164 --> 00:23:38.083
This isn't where our story should end.

00:23:38.875 --> 00:23:39.918
You're right.

00:23:40.001 --> 00:23:40.877
Understand?

00:23:43.839 --> 00:23:45.799
Yeah. I'll turn them down.

00:23:51.138 --> 00:23:52.556
Shop number ten!

00:23:53.515 --> 00:23:54.474
The last place.

00:23:54.558 --> 00:23:57.144
Time to throw my bad-luck kiss.

00:23:57.227 --> 00:23:58.395
This is the icing on the cake.

00:23:58.478 --> 00:23:59.312
Right!

00:24:00.188 --> 00:24:01.481
Welcome.

00:24:07.445 --> 00:24:08.655
That's what I like.

00:24:09.906 --> 00:24:11.283
Right!

00:24:13.702 --> 00:24:15.996
Damn. Talk about sparkly.

00:24:16.079 --> 00:24:18.623
Awesome. Take that too.

00:24:18.707 --> 00:24:20.625
This is the last place, so may as well.

00:24:21.251 --> 00:24:23.170
Hey! We're outta time!

00:24:25.881 --> 00:24:27.966
Crap! We gotta split!

00:26:12.487 --> 00:26:17.492
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
